    description: "Source: a second outside reader (a fresh LLM session given only the help output and the cached files) reviewed a hypergumbo 9.2.0 self-run on 2026-11-13, cache f36c63310c791188/results/c872eb7a7e793eab/ac34c56c06ec1788, made after the fixes from the first review merged. Each claim was re-checked against those files and the code on dev fed15705d7, then measured on 20 repositories that are not hypergumbo (default sketch and --no-source, 8k/32k/128k). Scripts, the 120 sketches and results.txt: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/outside_reader_review2_11142026.\n\nOBSERVED. The first line of the self-run sketch reads: \"hypergumbo is a local-first CLI that generates surveys and sketches from source code. The goal of this project is to efficiently help developers and LLMs understand a codebase. > Requires Python 3.10+.\" The last sentence is a README blockquote, with its marker. That is the sample string in the statement of INV-modor-vokot-vozus-nalom-mufir-pitig-pogun-rihum, closed satisfied on 2026-07-11. On knex (1 of the 20 other repositories measured) the marker leaks the other way round: the summary reads \"[knex.js](https://knex.github.io/documentation/) > **A SQL query builder that is _flexible_, _portable_, and _fun_ to use!** ...\". There the blockquote IS the project's one-line description, so a rule that skips every blockquote (what the heuristic does since INV-modor) would lose it; the title link and the bold markers are printed raw as well.\n\nMECHANISM. sketch._extract_readme_description tries sketch_embeddings.extract_readme_description_embedding first and falls back to _extract_readme_description_heuristic. INV-modor's fix put the blockquote skip in the heuristic only. Called directly on this repository's README on dev fed15705d7: the heuristic returns the two description sentences; the embedding function returns them followed by three blockquotes (\"> Requires Python 3.10+. ...\", \"> Installing on a personal machine? ...\", \"> Intel Mac users: ...\") and the word \"Output:\"; the 300-character truncation then cuts at the first sentence end. The embedding path runs whenever sentence-transformers is installed, which it is in the development environment and for anyone who ran install-embeddings.\n\nASK. One statement of which README text is description prose, applied before either extractor sees the text, so the two paths cannot differ on it: markup is removed (blockquote markers, emphasis, link syntax), and a block is kept or dropped by what it says, not by whether it is quoted (knex's tagline is a blockquote; this repository's three callouts are too). Test both paths on the same fixture; the embedding path can be tested without a model by giving the selection step fixed scores.\n\nGENERALITY (owner, 2026-11-13). The fix must be a rule that holds for any repository and any language. The hypergumbo self-run is only where the defect was first seen. A fix keyed to this repository's paths or file names, or one that works for one language only, does not close this item.\nMarkdown is not the only README format the extractors read; state the rule per format the reader supports (Markdown blockquote, reStructuredText admonition and note directives, AsciiDoc admonition blocks) or record which formats are not covered."  # b08e
